{"reference":"Luke 7","book":"Luke","chapter":7,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"historical_context","title":"The Woman’s Identity","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Luke calls the woman “a sinner,” but does not specify that her sin was sexual or identify her as Mary Magdalene. The scene instead centers on forgiveness, her acts of hospitality and love, and Simon’s judgment of her.","verse_refs":["Luke 7:36-50"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_luke_007_0dd57a2be2bf10a957c8e380"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}